 of you know cool  stuff going on for them today  and  i think a lot of these are younger  people  they have a lot of um  uh  tramping and yelling and shouting and  you know laughing and stuff like that  which used to bother me but now i  realize uh since last night it really  doesn't in part i think because i look  back on my own college  years and how how you know i did exactly  the same sort of thing  and didn't really you know what would i  have done if um i knew that there was  some  uh older professor next door  who's a visiting scholar probably not  cared that much and and i i didn't  actually we we probably made life  helpful  the uh the people who were you know  stuck dealing with us so um  in any case  got some good work done today i went uh  to the  library  got some some reading done i actually  had something kind of cool happen i  one of the dissertations that i was  reading was really great and it was by  this guy  um  tareo ferrara um who was a  jesuit  and i wanted to see if he was still  alive  his dissertation was from i think um  1970 something so i thought probably not  you know he'd have to be really young  to to write it then um  turns out actually i found his his  obituary he died in 1987.  61 years old um  and he he was a philosophy teacher he  taught philosophy  at a bunch of different places and then  um went on to earn his his doctorate he  wrote a really great dissertation about  anselm and reason and intellect and you  know all these these sorts of things  um so that was a lot of fun to do that i  spent a lot of the day um  working on on anselm related papers that  i've got going  and managed to bring something that i've  had long hanging for a while to fruition  and get that sent  to somebody did some reading in the st  thomas preparatory for my um working on  my piece on anger and leadership for  this upcoming conference  and now i also did some some some work  on epicurean philosophy got to  read some stuff of philodemus that they  had in the library  um turns out that he he actually wrote  these little short you know  six line sometimes eight line poems a  lot of which had to do with  you know what we might call typical  issues of pleasure for a  a fairly young to middle-aged man  a lot of really cool stuff in in those  and i found one that actually did have  to do with anger so i'm going to  incorporate that into the talk that i'm  working on for next saturday  um  tonight the rest of the night it's nine  o'clock now  uh i think i'm probably going to work  another  hour or two on my presentation for next  saturday i've got my epicurean materials  here  and so i'm going to  flesh out the talk  with the epicurus portions uh and if i  get to it the philidamus portions  the  um  cicero  portions as well which are not actually  cicero so much as people cicero knew the  the  on the ends  and  um  if i can get that done tonight that  means that i can start tomorrow  essentially with a full day  where i've got  a couple projects off the docket  and i don't have to go to the library at  all i don't have to work on the  dissertation stuff at all i can just  focus on the things that i came up here  to to work on  so if i can  get this knocked out that would really  be a great help  so on alumni night they have fireworks  and um  as soon as i heard them i went out to  the parking lot so i could  watch them and  this is uh  what i got to see  nice little display  right now we're getting towards the end  of it  and there were quite a few kids out  there as well all sitting down on the  grass a few  were adventurous and climbed up onto a  container  so here we get some of the the cool  stuff going on  i've always loved fireworks since i was  a kid actually fourth of july used to be  my my favorite holiday i suppose if i  was able to shoot off fireworks it  probably still could be  but i live in a state where we don't  really get to do much of anything and we  only get to watch what other people do  but in an